rting points though, much appreciated). I've tried to expose them to his little fanatical slice of heaven, inviting them to participate in seasonal rites that would align with many of their seasonal courts, asking for aid in dealing with problems, etc., but there has been no real interest in it. Could be I'm not pushing the right buttons, or they just are more interested in a changeling focused game despite the multi-splat venue. Cause at this point he wouldn't seem to be much more than a friendly werewolf that is trying to get them to work with him on stuff.<br /> <br /> Its possible that despite it how I feel in regards to my character fitting into the setting established by the storyteller, he just doesn't fit in to the setting/story the other players are trying to develop. I'd like to try and salvage it, but it may just come down to him not being a good fit, or just needing to force the other characters into having to interact with mine.<br /> <br /> Hopefully that answers most of your questions, admittedly was a bit much for me to digest, but I think I hit the high points.<br /> <br /> <br /> As far as I'm aware, I don't think there are any forsaken powers that would force their mask to drop, barring some sort of carefully considered spirit influence via a fetish, talen, spirit ally, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28146-dioeon","name":"DioEon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T18:39:03-07:00","id":1519301,"title":"","content":"Forcing a Mask to drop is an excessive tool for the scenario, I wouldn't take that as a serious recommendation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T18:43:31-07:00","id":1519302,"title":"","content":"Yea, I couldn't think of a situation where it'd organically occur to the point where my character would have pre-planned it. Interesting to consider from a purely mechanical standpoint though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28146-dioeon","name":"DioEon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T03:00:02-07:00","id":1519321,"title":"","content":"You haven't mentioned what the congregation actually believes in. What is their dogma and how in line with reality is it? The Fire-Touched Ban forces the Tribe to confront untruths, but most of them have a cultural blind spot where &quot;Truth is what I believe in and if facts disagree with that then the facts are wrong&quot;. If you haven't drafted a philosophy of the congregation yet, then this is a great opportunity to draft one most appropriate for the game. I like Shadowcatx's idea where the werewolf would demand radical honesty in all things (something super risky for Changelings), and he could also provide unflinching protection to the truthful. The Fire-touched would start as a possible ally, and as the game progresses, he could become gradually more demanding and impractical (or mellow out through actions of other PCs).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T05:09:39-07:00","id":1519333,"title":"","content":"That's a good suggestion, I've got several documents already written up for things like his pack, town, etc., and I've always been a bigger fan of roleplay power over mechanical. Forsaken provides a good opportunity to that as general actions can strengthen or weaken spirits without much need to involve mechanics. For example currently battling it out with a spirit of darkness that wishes to consume the light of his village. Been running a lot of seasonal rites and such with a heavy theme of fire and light. But further expanding on his belief system and giving it a real codified set of beliefs would probably go a long way in terms of what I like to utilize in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28146-dioeon","name":"DioEon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T08:15:03-07:00","id":1519429,"title":"","content":"In case anyone was interested, I did come up with something to build around as far as a system of beliefs or code. It is written from an IC point of view, and does need a bit more work, I think an introductory paragraph akin to a speech or sermon would be nice, bit of cleaning up on the wording and language, but the core idea I think is established:<br /> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>The Word of Fire</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cVery truly I tell you, everyone who lies is a slave to those lies. Listen to these words then you will know the truth, and the truth will set you free.\u201d ~ Isib Ur, the Prophet of Fire</i><br /> <br /> <b>&lt;Insert Introductory Paragraph here&gt;<br /> <br /> <br /> The Blazing Sacraments</b><br /> <i>Live the truth, this is our divine order.<br /> <br /> Pay falsehoods with penance, burning it away with fire of the flesh and soul.<br /> <br /> Stoke the fires of your soul, feed it the truth.<br /> <br /> Honor the manifestation of this fire, treat it reverently.<br /> <br /> Pity those who live in deceit, but rejoice for they can be saved.<br /> <br /> Do not seek out, or bear witness to those who do not live the truth, except to bring them our word.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Choir of Fire</b><br /> <i>The choir is the social arm of the faith, they travel amongst the people doing good works in its name. Leading by example, they live the truth and seek to strengthen it by the witnessing of their virtues.</i><b> <br /> <br /> The Clergy of Fire<br /> T</b><i>he clergy leads in the rituals of the faith, with which our fires are strengthened and forge our community stronger. Their ceremony is one of the foundations upon which we change the world.</i><b> <br /> <br /> The Templars of Fire</b><br /> <i>The templars protect our faith from those who would seek to destroy us and the truth, for some can only achieve absolution in death. They protect us through the strength of their faith, but their mercy we grant only as a last resort.</i><br /> <br /> <b>The People of Fire</b><br /> <i>Our people are our most treasured of the faith, they fight the true battle armed only with their belief in the truth. They live each day in service of our faith, and raise a new generation in service to our belief. </i></span><br /> <br /> <br /> </div> <br /> Still kinda considering how he'd work with/against changelings but one hand he would recognize their deceit being born of fear, something he could remedy as he offers protection to those who abandon lies and deceit for favor of living a true life. Even if as a werewolf he'd know very little about them or the True Fae, so believing he could protect them might not be smart from an out of character standpoint, but in character would be something he would believe however na\u00efve it may be. On the other hand, changelings are creatures irreversibly changed by the True Fae, who would be a sort of being representing concepts that are the polar opposite to the ideas of truth. If they cannot abandon the trappings of falsehood instilled in them by the True Fae, they much like their masters, can only &quot;achieve absolution in death&quot;.<br /> <br /> Obviously got a bit more tightening up to do on the concept, but just wanted to say thanks to folks for giving me a bit more to work with, expanding my knowledge base on the subject, and helping by asking me the right questions I myself need to answer.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28146-dioeon","name":"DioEon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}